Log JSON fields: timestamp, `requestId`, trace ID, method, **route template**, status, duration, content lengths, error code, non-PHI client ID. Do not log raw URIs, query strings, `Authorization`, cookies, patient IDs, or bodies. Allowlist headers only (`User-Agent`, `Content-Type`, `Accept`).

Sampling to stay under budget:
- 100% of 5xx and slow requests >1s
- 100% of 4xx with sanitized error code
- ~1% of successful 2xx requests, sampled by `requestId` hash
- Elasticsearch ILM retention 7–14 days, with index size alerts

For client debugging, return `X-Request-ID` in responses/errors so support can search logs. Use the separate audit log for patient identifiers. If deeper diagnostics are ever required, require explicit opt-in, redaction, and short retention — never default body capture.

